# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF line endings on every
# platform. The shell installers and templates under packaging/ are executed
# on Linux and embedded by tools/release-index, so a CRLF checkout on Windows
# would change their bytes and break both the tests and the shipped scripts.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets are never normalised.
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
*.icns binary

# Unified diffs legitimately contain lines that look like whitespace errors.
*.patch -whitespace
